## Then

1. **Watch the fleet.** In the Votal portal, open Enterprise Controls, then
   Device DLP. Laptops appear as they enroll, usually within minutes of the
   installer and profile arriving.
2. **Look at what monitor mode records.** Fleets are in monitor mode unless
   you have set them to enforce: nothing is blocked, every decision is
   recorded.
3. **Turn on enforcement.** When the results look right, set the fleet to
   `enforce` in the DLP policy on the same page.

## If something is wrong

On a laptop, as an administrator, `votal-device-agent verify` prints one line
per check with the reason for any failure. The health check in this kit shows
the same result in your MDM. The admin guide covers each failure:
https://docs.shield.votal.ai/device-dlp-agent/

## Later

- **A new kit:** download one from the portal. Upload its profile over this
  one (same identifier) and revoke this kit there.
- **Reinstalling a laptop:** revoke its old device in the portal first if it
  reported in the last 24 hours.
